Origin of the name Jemez
First recorded in 1830, the name Jemez is derived from the Spanish word "jemez" which means "place of the sun".
Early Origins of the Jemez family
The surname Jemez was first found in the county of Jemez, where they held a family seat from very ancient times. The first recorded spelling of the family name is shown to be that of William Jemez, which was dated 1276, in the "Census of the County of Jemez", during the reign of King Henry 11, known as "The Great", 1276 - 1307. Surnames became necessary when governments introduced personal taxation. In England this was known as Poll Tax. Throughout the centuries, surnames in every country have continued to "develop" often leading to astonishing variants of the original spelling.
